  "reasoning": "This commit introduced the buggy isMounted state management: it added `isMounted.set(NativeMethods.DokanRemoveMountPoint(...))` in shutdown(), which incorrectly sets isMounted to true (the return value semantics of DokanRemoveMountPoint are inverted relative to what the code assumed), causing the \"unable to unmount\" behavior and the log message wrongly stating the device is unmounted. It also introduced the unconditional `isMounted.set(true)` after starting DokanMain without properly synchronizing with the asynchronous mount completion, which is the root cause the fix commit addresses by wrapping the call in a CompletableFuture with a timeout and only setting isMounted based on the actual mountStatus. The subsequent commit 08ec099de587 only added a TODO comment (non-semantic), confirming 4473d460b995 as the actual bug-introducing commit.",
